{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}AlmaLinux 9 in WSL2 : install PHP, Apache, MariaDB, Composer, PhpMyadmin{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">How to's</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">AlmaLinux 9 in WSL2 : install PHP, Apache, MariaDB, Composer, PhpMyadmin</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this article we will demonstrate how we install AlmaLinux 9 using Windows Subsystem for Linux  (WSL2).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>First, you need to check if your machine is ready for using WSL2. Open Windows Terminal and execute the following command:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>wsl -v</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The output should look similar to this:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code><strong>WSL version: 2.2.4.0</strong>
Kernel version: 5.15.153.1-2
WSLg version: 1.0.61
MSRDC version: 1.2.5326
Direct3D version: 1.611.1-81528511
DXCore version: 10.0.26091.1-240325-1447.ge-release
Windows version: 10.0.22631.3737</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If instead of the above output, you get an error, it means that WSL is not (completely) installed on your machine. In this case, please follow the instructions found in <a href="https://docs.dotkernel.org/development/v1/setup/installation/" data-type="URL" data-id="https://github.com/dotkernel/development/blob/main/wsl/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">this guide</a>, then return to this page and continue with the next step.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Download and install AlmaLinux 9</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Open Microsoft Store and search for <code>AlmaLinux</code>. From the results, select <code>AlmaLinux 9</code> and install it. Once installed, clicking on <em>Open</em> will open it in Windows Terminal.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The installer will prompt you for your <em>username</em>, your <em>password</em> and <em>password confirmation</em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Setup AlmaLinux 9</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While still in the AlmaLinux 9 terminal, start executing the following commands.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Install required packages:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>sudo dnf install epel-release dnf-utils http://rpms.remirepo.net/enterprise/remi-release-9.rpm -y</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Update installed packages:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>sudo dnf upgrade -y</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Install Ansible:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>sudo dnf install ansible -y</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Clone our development environment setup package:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>git clone https://github.com/dotkernel/development.git</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Navigate to the directory with the Ansible recipes:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>cd ~/development/wsl/</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using your preferred text editor, open <strong>config.yml</strong> where you must fill in the empty fields. Save and close the file.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Run Step 1 of the installer script (it will prompt you for the password you entered during the installation process):</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>ansible-playbook -i hosts install.yml --ask-become-pass</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Restart AlmaLinux 9:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>press <code>Control</code> + <code>d</code></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Open Windows Terminal</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>stop AlmaLinux 9 by executing <code>wsl -t AlmaLinux9</code></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>start AlmaLinux 9 by executing <code>wsl -d AlmaLinux9</code></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Navigate back to the directory with the Ansible recipes:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>cd ~/development/wsl/</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Run Step 2 of the installer script (once again, it will prompt you for the password you entered during the installation process):</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code>ansible-playbook -i hosts install.yml --ask-become-pass</code></pre>
<!-- /wp:code -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once finished, the installation is complete, your AlmaLinux 9 development environment is ready to use.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Test AlmaLinux 9</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Check if everything works by opening in your browser:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>http://localhost/ - Apache's default home page</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>http://localhost/info.php - PHP info page</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>http://localhost/phpmyadmin/ - PhpMyAdmin (login with username <strong>root</strong> + the root password you configured in <strong>config.yml</strong> under mariadb -&gt; <em>root_password</em>)</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The complete guide with additional features is available <a href="https://docs.dotkernel.org/development/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">here</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
{% endblock %}